%description:

Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass:reno -- Reno halves the window, and a partial ACK ends its recovery.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the NED type of the algorithm of each connection"; TcpReno is the fast
recovery of RFC 5681, which a partial ACK ends.

The classes: the nine algorithms of the package inet.transportlayer.tcp.flavours (TcpNewReno is
the default, TcpReno the value of LegacyTcp, TcpCubic of LinuxTcp), qualified-alias (a
qualified NED type name), unknown (a name without a NED type: an error) and socket-override
(the open command of a socket selects another algorithm). Each test of an algorithm checks a
behavior that none of the other eight algorithms shows. The code:
TcpConnection::createTcpAlgorithm() and the classes of the algorithms. This test separates TcpReno: TcpNewReno, TcpCubic and TcpTahoe retransmit the second hole at
the partial ACK, DcTcp sends its SYN with ECT, TcpCubic reduces to 0.7 of the window,
TcpVegas sets no threshold at a fast retransmit, and TcpNoCongestionControl and DumbTcp have
no fast retransmit.

Host under test: host1, without SACK and with tcpEcnMode "rfc3168" (preconditions: ECN shows
DcTcp, which is TcpReno without ECN), which sends 100000 bytes; the round trip is 40 ms, and
the tap drops the 15th and the 17th data segment once. Observation: level 1, the SYN of
host1 is Not-ECT; level 2, the first slow-start threshold is about half the window; level 1,
host1 retransmits the second hole only after three ACKs of it: the partial ACK and two
duplicate ACKs, a second fast retransmit.

%# parameter: Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# class: reno
%# value: "TcpReno"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAlgorithmClassReno")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 14 * 1448 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).drop()
                     .describe("the 15th data segment of host1, the first time"))
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 16 * 1448 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).drop()
                     .describe("the 17th data segment of host1, the first time"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host2.eth[0].mac").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("ipv4.ecn == 0")
             .describe("the SYN of host1 at host2, Not-ECT")
             .within(0.5))
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host1.tcp").signal("cwnd")
                                        .captureMax("cwndBefore", "value")
                                        .within(4.0)))
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
                                        .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.ackNo == {isn} + 1 + 16 * 1448")
                                        .captureCount("acksOfSecondHole")
                                        .describe("each ACK of the second hole")
                                        .within(4.0)))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("ssthresh")
                  .filterValueAtMost(1e8)
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      double ratio = context.event.value / context.get("cwndBefore").doubleValue();
                      return ratio >= 0.3 && ratio <= 0.55;
                  })
                  .describe("the slow-start threshold at the loss, about half the window")
                  .within(1.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 16 * 1448 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("{acksOfSecondHole} >= 3")
             .describe("the retransmission of the second hole, after three ACKs of it")
             .within(1.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAlgorithmClassReno compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "TcpReno"    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100000B
*.host1.tcp.sackSupport = false
*.host1.tcp.tcpEcnMode = "rfc3168"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAlgorithmClassReno: PASS
